1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,342
Here's the part of travel planning nobody

2
00:00:02,347 --> 00:00:05,262
likes: explaining yourself all over again.

3
00:00:05,377 --> 00:00:06,487
The quiet room.

4
00:00:06,492 --> 00:00:07,642
The morning light.

5
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:09,703
The road noise that ruined your last

6
00:00:09,708 --> 00:00:10,463
stay.

7
00:00:10,578 --> 00:00:12,704
Those small details matter.

8
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:20,468
So I built Anghkooey, an AI concierge

9
00:00:20,473 --> 00:00:22,157
whose name means remember.

10
00:00:22,563 --> 00:00:24,427
With your permission, it keeps the small

11
00:00:24,432 --> 00:00:26,854
details behind your choices and brings them

12
00:00:26,859 --> 00:00:28,241
back when they're relevant.

13
00:00:28,565 --> 00:00:30,075
Watch what changes.

14
00:00:38,350 --> 00:00:40,400
Before linking, I ask about a traveller's

15
00:00:40,405 --> 00:00:41,752
hotel preferences.

16
00:00:42,077 --> 00:00:44,620
Anghkooey won't guess from what's available here.

17
00:00:45,119 --> 00:00:47,261
In Telegram, I enable memory and share

18
00:00:47,266 --> 00:00:51,162
what matters: quiet hotels, beautiful natural light,

19
00:00:51,167 --> 00:00:53,421
and no rooms facing busy roads.

20
00:00:53,687 --> 00:00:55,243
The preference is acknowledged.

21
00:00:55,649 --> 00:00:57,780
A separate Web save shows a confirmed

22
00:00:57,785 --> 00:00:59,156
Walrus receipt.

23
00:01:05,350 --> 00:01:07,394
First, the connection is confirmed.

24
00:01:07,718 --> 00:01:10,122
Now I ask about my saved preferences.

25
00:01:10,447 --> 00:01:12,497
This time, Anghkooey doesn't make me repeat

26
00:01:12,502 --> 00:01:13,420
the story.

27
00:01:13,686 --> 00:01:16,485
It recalls quiet hotels and natural lighting,

28
00:01:16,693 --> 00:01:18,505
two durable preferences.

29
00:01:18,829 --> 00:01:21,477
The actual reply makes the change visible.

30
00:01:21,801 --> 00:01:23,805
It also honestly flags what it can't

31
00:01:23,810 --> 00:01:27,224
confirm about where those preferences were shared.

32
00:01:31,350 --> 00:01:33,243
People don't live in one tab.

33
00:01:33,568 --> 00:01:36,297
Anghkooey works through Telegram and iMessage.

34
00:01:36,621 --> 00:01:39,159
From Profile, I generate a one-time linking

35
00:01:39,164 --> 00:01:41,916
code and confirm through the messaging channel.

36
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:45,735
Existing accounts require an explicit merge confirmation.

37
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:48,330
Once linked, those preferences can follow me

38
00:01:48,335 --> 00:01:50,020
across conversations.

39
00:01:56,350 --> 00:01:58,649
Memory also needs a way to change.

40
00:01:58,974 --> 00:02:00,966
In the Memories library, I can review

41
00:02:00,971 --> 00:02:04,042
confirmed records, search for relevant facts, and

42
00:02:04,047 --> 00:02:05,929
correct an outdated preference.

43
00:02:06,427 --> 00:02:08,762
A correction creates a new Walrus blob

44
00:02:08,808 --> 00:02:11,101
and retires the previous version from future

45
00:02:11,106 --> 00:02:11,920
recall.

46
00:02:12,244 --> 00:02:14,602
Saving memory starts with permission.

47
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:23,412
Underneath: DeepSeek Flash, memory orchestration, Walrus,

48
00:02:23,493 --> 00:02:25,880
Neon for account state, and a persistent

49
00:02:25,885 --> 00:02:27,511
Photon messaging worker.

50
00:02:27,916 --> 00:02:31,969
The engineering challenges were real: ESM-only SDK

51
00:02:31,992 --> 00:02:36,178
imports, missing peer packages, reasoning tokens consuming

52
00:02:36,183 --> 00:02:38,912
response budgets, and duplicate workers.

53
00:02:39,236 --> 00:02:41,880
We addressed them and documented the lessons.

54
00:02:42,350 --> 00:02:43,721
No fake bookings.

55
00:02:43,766 --> 00:02:45,706
No memory claims without proof.

56
00:02:46,205 --> 00:02:48,336
A concierge that remembers what matters and

57
00:02:48,341 --> 00:02:49,479
lets you correct it.

58
00:02:49,885 --> 00:02:50,930
Anghkooey.

59
00:02:51,255 --> 00:02:53,682
You shouldn't have to explain yourself twice.
